cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PreVisS-Net in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PreVisS-Net: A Multimodal, Domain-Generalizable Pre-Visual Stress Sensing Network for UAV-Based Early Detection of Crop Stress"
authors:
  - family-names: "Research Consortium"
    given-names: "PreVisS-Net"
    affiliation: "Precision Agriculture & Remote Sensing Laboratory"
version: "1.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.10827394"
date-released: "2026-08-28"
license: "MIT"
repository-code: "https://github.com/previssnet/previssnet"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.10827394"
keywords:
  - "pre-visual crop stress"
  - "multispectral UAV remote sensing"
  - "domain generalization"
  - "temporal vision transformer"
  - "water stress early detection"
  - "crop water stress index (CWSI)"
  - "edge deployment"
abstract: >-
  PreVisS-Net is an open-source deep learning framework for UAV-based pre-visual
  detection of agricultural crop water, nutritional, and heat stress. By combining
  multimodal spatial cross-attention (AFAM), temporal sequence modeling via ViT
  Transformers, and domain-adversarial feature alignment (GRL), PreVisS-Net delivers
  an early-warning lead time of 18.5 days prior to physical symptom manifestation
  while maintaining robust zero-shot cross-domain transfer (mean generalization gap 7.8 pts).
